  "verdict": "Measured: Zn-HAp (one Zn-substituted cell) on a (TiO2)16 cluster has 116 atoms and 1844 basis functions at 21e's tier (1546 with LANL2DZ on the 3d metals, 3468 at def2-TZVP); PEDOT:PSS as the doped polaron on the same cluster has 154 atoms, 1099 electrons (a doublet) and 1932 functions. The pipeline's largest routine SCF at 21e's tier is so2cf3 (904 functions, 1022 s) and at def2-TZVP 21f's so2cf3 (1989 functions, 2.8 h Os(II), 24.5 h Os(III)), so the clusters are 2.04× and 2.14× the 21e anchor and about the size of what def2-TZVP already ran. Estimated: the series scale as N^1.96 (21e) and N^1.97 (ωB97X); extrapolating with p from the fit to 3, one 21e-tier SCF of Zn-HAp/TiO2 takes 1.1–2.4 h and a relaxation 0.7–6 days; PEDOT:PSS (open-shell factor 1.3–2.23 from the series' routine UKS/RKS pairs) 1.6–6.2 h and 1.0–16 days. D3/D4 are not installed, but PySCF carries VV10 natively (ωB97X-V-type functionals), so a dispersion-inclusive calculation needs no new dependency; at def2-TZVP, the tier such a functional runs at, one SCF of Zn-HAp/TiO2 is 8–15 h and a relaxation 5–37 days (VV10's own grid cost not included). So a cluster relaxation of one adsorbate is within reach of our CPU — days to weeks, one job at a time; an adsorption energy is 3 such SCFs (5 with counterpoise). What it cannot settle is whether a cluster models the surface: a periodic slab is the usual model, and a cluster study needs its own size and termination convergence, which multiplies the jobs."
}
